WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.279
Around 1893 a family of Russian Jews fleeing

2
00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:08.891
persecution landed in New York with almost nothing.

3
00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:11.430
Their youngest son, a boy called Israel

4
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.292
Baline, would grow up to write "God Bless America."

5
00:00:14.642 --> 00:00:20.609
Berlin was born Israel Baline on 11 May 1888 in the Russian Empire.

6
00:00:20.959 --> 00:00:23.525
The exact town is genuinely uncertain.

7
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:27.647
His father died while Israel was still a boy, and he left school to

8
00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:31.363
help support the family, selling newspapers and singing for coins.

9
00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:34.479
He became a singing waiter in the saloons of the Bowery,

10
00:00:34.479 --> 00:00:37.542
and there began putting his own words to the tunes of the day.

11
00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:42.269
A printer set his name on the sheet music as "I. Berlin," and he kept it.

12
00:00:42.619 --> 00:00:45.432
In 1911 "Alexander's Ragtime Band" made

13
00:00:45.432 --> 00:00:48.389
him famous on both sides of the Atlantic.

14
00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:52.407
Berlin took his oath as a United States citizen on

15
00:00:52.407 --> 00:00:56.076
6 February 1918, after several years of paperwork.

16
00:00:56.426 --> 00:00:58.771
Within months the new citizen was drafted.

17
00:00:59.121 --> 00:01:01.890
It was around this time, too, that he first drafted a

18
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.286
patriotic song he judged too solemn, and put it away in a drawer.

19
00:01:05.636 --> 00:01:08.911
In 1938, with war returning to Europe,

20
00:01:08.911 --> 00:01:12.962
Berlin took that song back out and reworked it.

21
00:01:13.312 --> 00:01:16.900
The singer Kate Smith introduced "God Bless America"

22
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.556
on the radio on 11 November 1938, and Berlin assigned

23
00:01:20.556 --> 00:01:24.144
its royalties to a fund for the Boy and Girl Scouts.

24
00:01:24.494 --> 00:01:27.047
Four years later, in the film Holiday Inn, he

25
00:01:27.047 --> 00:01:30.055
introduced "White Christmas," which became one of the

26
00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:33.573
best-selling songs ever recorded and won him an Academy Award.

27
00:01:33.923 --> 00:01:36.733
He said this the same year he brought out "God Bless America":

28
00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:39.847
“I'd like to write a great peace song, but it's hard

29
00:01:39.847 --> 00:01:42.313
to do, because you have trouble dramatizing peace.”

30
00:01:42.913 --> 00:01:44.794
Why might someone who arrived as a

31
00:01:44.794 --> 00:01:47.395
newcomer write the songs a whole country sings?
